#extend("layouts/base"):
#export("body"):
<!--
  M9 (/privacy). Placeholder body text by the user's decision -- see
  LegalWebController's doc comment for why the legacy app's policy wasn't
  carried over. The version stamp is real: it's LegalVersions.privacyPolicy,
  the same constant AuthService records as User.privacyPolicyVersion on
  every new account (criterion #7). Section headings are the topics the
  final policy needs to cover (architecture §13); only their wording is
  placeholder.
-->
<div class="ds-page-head">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><span class="ds-version">Version #(version)</span></p>
</div>

<div class="card ds-prose">
    <div class="ds-alert ds-alert-info">This page is a placeholder. The final Privacy Policy is still being written.</div>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Placeholder.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>Placeholder.</p>

    <h2>Who processes it</h2>
    <p>Placeholder.</p>
    <p>Profile photos: if you sign in with Google, your Google profile photo is shown by default; it's loaded from Google's servers by the browser of anyone viewing a page with your photo, so Google receives their request. Gravatar is only used if you choose it on your <a href="/account">account page</a>: we then ask gravatar.com whether your email address has one, and viewers' browsers load it from gravatar.com, which receives an encoded (hashed) form of your email address. Photos you upload are stored by us, with location and camera details removed. You can choose a different photo or show none at any time.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Placeholder.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Placeholder. You can already download your data or ask us to delete your account from your <a href="/account">account page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:support@expatevents.net">support@expatevents.net</a>.</p>

    <h2>Credits</h2>
    <p>Event time zones are worked out from time zone boundary data by <a href="https://github.com/evansiroky/timezone-boundary-builder">timezone-boundary-builder</a>, © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/">Open Database License (ODbL)</a>.</p>
</div>
#endexport
#endextend
